```

Hmm wait, `internal` here is already the serialized path like "/manufacturer", so result "#/manufacturer". With my custom serializer producing "manufacturer" (no leading /), result would be "#manufacturer". 

So hrefs from routerLink would be "#manufacturer" ✓ (contains "manufacturer" ✓ and clicking navigates to hash "#manufacturer", hashchange fires, Location picks it up, router parses "manufacturer" ✓).

This is doable but relies on Angular internals of Angular 18.2. Let me actually check the Angular 18.2 source in node_modules to confirm HashLocationStrategy behavior.

